  "details": "A flaw in Node.js HTTP/2 handling allows `nghttp2_session_mem_send()` to be called re-entrantly while `nghttp2_session_mem_recv()` is executing, resulting in a heap-use-after-free.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability affects Node.js **26.x**, **24.x**, and **22.x**.",
